# v309 — THE DUPLICATE PREVIEWS RETIRE
#
# The application-side consolidation of the authority v308 established. Both
# preview projections stop deriving availability and start rendering it:
# event_workspace.next_actions and event_stage_detail.next_actions are the same
# projection, availability_lifecycle_actions(), reading canonical
# available_actions. Blocker vocabulary comes from the ladder's declared
# subject_path and ground instead of literal lists.
#
# Successor migration: CREATE OR REPLACE of two v276/v279-era projections plus
# three read-only helpers and the marker. No ceremony, no v306/v307a/v307b/v308
# object, and no table, index, trigger, policy or grant is touched. The v308
# authority functions are provably unaware of this release.
#
# Nothing externally observable is removed. next_actions keeps its array and its
# {action,label,available,reason} keys and gains reason_code; event_stage_detail
# keeps next_action and blockers and gains next_actions; event_workspace.blockers
# keeps {what,cause_ref,why,next_action}. available_actions and
# event_available_actions are unchanged.
release          v309
migration        supabase/v309_preview_consolidation.sql
migration_source repository
min_release      v308

superseded       event_workspace (next_actions is the canonical projection; declared kind set)
superseded       event_stage_detail (blockers and next_actions over declared grounds)

function         availability_lifecycle_actions(p_event uuid)
function         availability_obligation_kinds(p_action_key text)
function         availability_declared_ground(p_action_key text, p_condition text)
function         v309_preview_consolidation()
